-- title:
--   Right-invariance of the Kummer cocycle under stabilisers of α
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $\alpha$ be a unit of $L$, and let $\sigma,\tau$ be $K$-algebra automorphisms of $L$, subject to the single hypothesis that $\tau$ fixes $\alpha$, i.e. $\tau(\alpha)=\alpha$ as an equality in $L$ (stated for the underlying element of $L$, not directly in $L^\times$). Here `kummerCocycle` is the function sending a $K$-algebra automorphism $\rho$ of $L$ to the unit $(\rho \bullet \alpha)/\alpha$ of $L^\times$, where $\bullet$ is the natural action of the automorphism group on $L^\times$. The conclusion is the equality of units
--   $$\frac{(\sigma\tau)\bullet\alpha}{\alpha} \;=\; \frac{\sigma\bullet\alpha}{\alpha}$$
--   in $L^\times$, that is, `kummerCocycle α (σ * τ) = kummerCocycle α σ`, where the product $\sigma * \tau$ is the group operation of $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$, acting as $\tau$ followed by $\sigma$. No finiteness, separability, normality or algebraicity assumption is made on $L/K$, and $\alpha$ is an arbitrary unit.
--
--   This records that the Kummer cochain $\rho \mapsto \rho(\alpha)/\alpha$ is right-invariant under the stabiliser of $\alpha$ in the group of $K$-algebra automorphisms of $L$, so that it factors through the coset space of that stabiliser. It is used for the variant phrased in terms of the fixing subgroup of the subalgebra generated by $\alpha$, [`groupCohomology.Kummer.kummerCocycle_mul_eq_of_mem_fixingSubgroup_adjoin`](thm.html#groupCohomology.Kummer.kummerCocycle_mul_eq_of_mem_fixingSubgroup_adjoin), and in the rank computation [`groupCohomology.finrank_continuousEquivariantHom_eq_finrank_invariants_linHom_dualTwist`](thm.html#groupCohomology.finrank_continuousEquivariantHom_eq_finrank_invariants_linHom_dualTwist), where local constancy of such cochains is what makes a continuity argument work.
